Package: vfs495-fprint
Version: 0.1.4
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: fprintd, libpam-fprintd, gdb, python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, gir1.2-fprint-2.0, libusb-0.1-4, 7zip | p7zip-full, curl | wget, ca-certificates, systemd
Maintainer: saifulmd0 <saifulmd0@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/saifulmd0/vfs495-linux
Description: Fingerprint login for the Validity VFS495 (138a:003f) reader
 Enables fingerprint authentication (login, sudo, screen unlock via fprintd + PAM)
 for the Validity Sensors VFS495 swipe reader found in 2013-2015 HP EliteBook,
 ProBook and ZBook laptops, which libfprint does not support natively.
 .
 On install it downloads HP's proprietary Validity Linux driver from HP's own
 server (not redistributed here), and sets up a capture service that feeds
 fprintd. After installing, run: fprintd-enroll
